#. type: Title #
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quarkus Minor Release Announcement"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step-by-step guide for creating a Quarkus minor release announcement blog\n"
"post.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概要"

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "A minor release announcement requires:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "A blog post in `content/posts/`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "An update to `_data/versions.yaml`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** The first release of a new minor series is not always `.0` — it\n"
"can be `.1` or higher (e.g. 3.39.1). The distinction between a minor and\n"
"micro announcement is whether this is the **first release of a new minor\n"
"series**, not whether the micro version is `0`. When in doubt, the user\n"
"will clarify.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1 — Gather Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before writing anything, collect all the data. Ask the user for:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The version number** (e.g. `3.39`)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The notable features** — the user will provide these, typically as\n"
"a list of PR numbers and descriptions\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The contributor count** from the GitHub UI (see below)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contributor count"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The count displayed on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus (Contributors\n"
"section in the right sidebar) **cannot be reliably obtained via the GitHub\n"
"API**:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The REST API `GET /repos/quarkusio/quarkus/contributors` is capped at\n"
"500 results.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The GraphQL `mentionableUsers` field includes all users with repo\n"
"access, not just contributors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**It must be obtained manually** by the user visiting\n"
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus and reading the number from the\n"
"\"Contributors\" link in the right sidebar.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contributor list"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run the following in the `../quarkus/` repository, adjusting the version\n"
"range:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git -C ../quarkus fetch upstream --tags\n"
"git -C ../quarkus shortlog -s '<previous>.0'..'<current>.<latest_micro>' \\\n"
"  | cut -d$'\\t' -f 2 \\\n"
"  | grep -v dependabot \\\n"
"  | grep -v quarkusbot \\\n"
"  | sort -d -f -i \\\n"
"  | paste -sd ',' - \\\n"
"  | sed 's/,/, /g'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **start** of the range is always the `.0` of the **previous** minor\n"
"(e.g. `3.38.0` when announcing 3.39).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **end** of the range is the **latest released micro** of the current\n"
"minor at the time of the announcement (e.g. `3.39.0`, or `3.39.2` if\n"
"micro releases have already been published). Check the tags to find the\n"
"latest micro.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Post-processing the contributor list:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:74
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Deduplicate names with diacritics/accents**: some contributors have\n"
"commits under both an ASCII and an accented version of their name\n"
"(e.g. `Phillip Kruger` / `Phillip Krüger`, or `brunobat` / `Bruno\n"
"Baptista`). Keep the version with diacritics/accents, or the real\n"
"name over a username when both exist.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Add `and ` before the last name** in the list.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "Platform component updates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare the previous and current minor branches of the\n"
"`quarkusio/quarkus-platform` repository:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"gh api repos/quarkusio/quarkus-platform/compare/<previous>...<current> \\\n"
"  --jq '.commits[].commit.message'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Filter for commits starting with `Update` or `Upgrade` (ignoring Quarkus\n"
"core upgrades, dependabot, and maven-release-plugin). For components not\n"
"covered by these commits (e.g. CXF, Flow), check the platform `pom.xml`\n"
"on the current branch to see if their versions changed:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"gh api repos/quarkusio/quarkus-platform/contents/pom.xml?ref=<current> \\\n"
"  --jq '.content' | base64 -d | grep -iE \"cxf|flow\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "When listing components, link to release notes when available:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Camel Quarkus**: `https://camel.apache.org/releases/q-<version>/`\n"
"— these are **not available** at Quarkus announcement time; they are\n"
"published later. Do not check or link them; just list the version.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quarkus CXF**: `https://docs.quarkiverse.io/quarkus-cxf/dev/release-notes/<version>.html`\n"
"(e.g. `https://docs.quarkiverse.io/quarkus-cxf/dev/release-notes/3.38.0.html`)\n"
"— these are typically available; link when they exist. If CXF went\n"
"through multiple versions (visible in the platform commit history),\n"
"check and link release notes for each intermediate version. Use the\n"
"term \"release notes\" (not \"changelog\") in link text to match the CXF\n"
"documentation terminology.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2 — Create the Blog Post"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "File location and naming"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the file at:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "content/posts/YYYY-MM-DD-quarkus-<major>-<minor>-released.adoc\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example: `content/posts/2026-09-30-quarkus-3-39-released.adoc`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "The date in the filename **must match** the `date` in the front matter.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "Front matter"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:124
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"---\n"
"layout: post\n"
"title: 'Quarkus <version> - <headline features summary>'\n"
"date: YYYY-MM-DD\n"
"tags: release\n"
"synopsis: 'We released Quarkus <version>, which comes with <brief feature list>.'\n"
"author: gsmet\n"
"---\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "`layout`: always `post`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "`tags`: always `release` for release announcements\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "`author`: must match a key in `_data/authors.yaml`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:141
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`title`: include the version and a comma-separated summary of the\n"
"most notable features (2-4 items)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "`synopsis`: one sentence summarizing what the release brings\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blog post structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:146
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Follow this exact structure (see recent posts in `content/posts/` for\n"
"reference):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (asciidoc)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're pleased to announce the release of Quarkus <version>.\n"
"\n"
"This release brings several notable features:\n"
"\n"
"* https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/<number>[#<number>] - <description>\n"
"* ...\n"
"\n"
"== Update\n"
"\n"
"To update to Quarkus <version>, we recommend updating to the latest version of the Quarkus CLI and run:\n"
"\n"
"[source,bash]\n"
"----\n"
"quarkus update\n"
"----\n"
"\n"
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus <version>.\n"
"\n"
"For more information about the adjustments you need to make to your applications, please refer to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-<version>[Quarkus <version> migration guide].\n"
"\n"
"== What's new?\n"
"\n"
"=== <Feature 1 title>\n"
"\n"
"<Description of feature 1>\n"
"\n"
"=== <Feature 2 title>\n"
"\n"
"<Description of feature 2>\n"
"\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"=== Platform updates\n"
"\n"
"Various Platform components were upgraded including:\n"
"\n"
"- <Component> to <version>\n"
"- ...\n"
"\n"
"== Full changelog\n"
"\n"
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/<version>.0.CR1[<version>.0.CR1] and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/<version>.0[<version>.0] on GitHub.\n"
"\n"
"== Contributors\n"
"\n"
"The Quarkus community is growing and has now https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/graphs/contributors[<count>] contributors.\n"
"Many many thanks to each and everyone of them.\n"
"\n"
"In particular for the <version> release, thanks to <contributor list>.\n"
"\n"
"== Come Join Us\n"
"\n"
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... Let's build something great together!\n"
"\n"
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our welcoming community:\n"
"\n"
" * provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];\n"
" * craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];\n"
" * discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];\n"
" * ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/quarkus[Stack Overflow].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:210
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notes on the structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:225
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The introductory paragraph can vary: if it's a lighter release (most\n"
"features going to the next major), say so. See recent posts for tone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:225
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bullet list at the top links PRs by number. Each item is a GitHub\n"
"PR link followed by a short description.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:225
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each feature in \"What's new?\" gets its own `===` subsection.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:225
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Platform updates go under their own `=== Platform updates` subsection,\n"
"with an optional `==== Component upgrades` sub-subsection, or an\n"
"`==== <Component name>` sub-subsection if a component deserves a\n"
"paragraph of description (e.g. a new addition to the platform).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:225
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When a platform component went through multiple version bumps (e.g.\n"
"CXF 3.39.0 → 3.39.1), list the **final version** as the upgrade\n"
"target, then link each version's release notes in parentheses:\n"
"`Quarkus CXF to 3.39.1 (link[3.39.0 release notes], link[3.39.1 release notes])`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:226
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3 — Update `_data/versions.yaml`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:230
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set `quarkus.version` to the new version and `quarkus.announce` to the\n"
"blog post path:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:231
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"quarkus:\n"
"  version: <version>.0\n"
"  announce: /blog/quarkus-<major>-<minor>-released/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:238
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example:\n"
msgstr "例えば、以下のようになります:"

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:239
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"quarkus:\n"
"  version: 3.39.0\n"
"  announce: /blog/quarkus-3-39-released/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:248
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only update `quarkus.version` and `quarkus.announce`. Do not touch\n"
"the other fields (`graalvm`, `jdk`, `maven`, `documentation`) unless\n"
"the user specifically asks.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4 — Preview"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:256
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After creating the post and updating versions, suggest the user preview\n"
"locally. The blog preview skill (`.agents/skills/building-blog/SKILL.md`)\n"
"has full instructions — but note that the preview infrastructure may\n"
"still be Jekyll-based. If `just blog-preview` or `blog-preview.sh` are\n"
"available, use them. Otherwise, the Roq dev mode can be started with:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:257
#, no-wrap
msgid "./mvnw quarkus:dev\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "Micro Release Announcements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:264
#, no-wrap
msgid "Micro releases (e.g. 3.38.3) are much simpler. The structure is:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "content/posts/YYYY-MM-DD-quarkus-<major>-<minor>-<micro>-released.adoc\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:270
#, no-wrap
msgid "Front matter:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:271
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"---\n"
"layout: post\n"
"title: 'Quarkus <version> - Maintenance release'\n"
"date: YYYY-MM-DD\n"
"tags: release\n"
"synopsis: 'We released Quarkus <version>, a regular maintenance release.'\n"
"author: gsmet\n"
"---\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:283
#, no-wrap
msgid "Body (much shorter, no feature descriptions or contributor list):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (asciidoc)
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:284
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Today, we released Quarkus <version>, a maintenance release for our <minor> release train.\n"
"\n"
"This release contains bugfixes and documentation improvements.\n"
"It should be a safe upgrade for anyone already using <minor>.\n"
"\n"
"== Update\n"
"\n"
"To update to Quarkus <minor>, we recommend updating to the latest version of the Quarkus CLI and run:\n"
"\n"
"[source,bash]\n"
"----\n"
"quarkus update\n"
"----\n"
"\n"
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus <minor>.\n"
"\n"
"For more information about the adjustments you need to make to your applications, please refer to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-<minor>[Quarkus <minor> migration guide].\n"
"\n"
"== Full changelog\n"
"\n"
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/<version>[<version>] on GitHub.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .agents/skills/release-announcement/SKILL.md:309
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For micro releases, also update `_data/versions.yaml` with the new\n"
"micro version number and set the announce path accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
